# #98: band is called on a value that is an int one time and a float the
# next. Spec 1.11 says a bit operator on anything but an int stops the
# program, so both v2 engines print 1 and then stop at the float. (The old
# route's `pat --patc` gave 62.)
make a function called bandtest takes f returns done
  print(f band 255)
end
bandtest(1)
bandtest(1.0 + 61.0)
